      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T06:33:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I said in\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4511814/43\nSeparating the test is meaningless, because the problem is not the test file.\n\nThe problem is in `common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands.cc`.\n\nIf we want to link `common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands.cc` in our test, this file will introduce `all` of the dependency problem.\n(Obviously, the test is meaningless if we don\u0027t link to the file that contains the function we want to test.)\n\nThe only way to resolve that issue is by adding another file called `common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands_without_driver_info.cc`. Did you prefer this solution?\n\nOr did you want `common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands_without_driver_info.cc` \u0026 `common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands_without_driver_info_and_reset_secret.cc`?",
